I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Fetching `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=…` would need `aap:caps/http-client`, which this node was not granted. Adding that import would widen the node's authority beyond its contract.

It would also send the untrusted item text to an outside host. And because the output must stay the same, the fetched result could never be used anyway. If you need enrichment, add an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` capability to the node's `with` clause in the graph, and I can then write it in.

